WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.320
Only one thing about Todd Phillips' standalone
Joker movie is certain: this isn't going to

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:06.900
be any old superhero film.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.740
Here are all the reasons why it's time to
get hyped about this brand new take on the

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.080
Dark Knight's greatest nemesis.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.360
First things first: this isn't a Batman movie.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.990
Sure, Bruce Wayne has been cast, but in this
movie he's a child with no idea what's still

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:21.520
to come.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.180
He's not the focus, the protagonist, or even
a major player.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.540
This is a story about the Joker and the world
that made him.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.000
But just as the greatest Batman stories are
often about the kind of evil he faces down,

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.960
so too might this story be about the good
that the Joker fights.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:39.480
That means this film isn't just capable of
being a great Joker story, but also a great

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.710
story about Gotham itself, too.

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:46.430
And that's a perspective even fans of the
comics rarely get to see.

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:51.359
Legendary actors aren't new to superhero movies,
and even the Joker himself has been portrayed

00:00:51.359 --> 00:00:52.800
by some world-class performers.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:57.160
“Let's put a smile on that face."

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:01.090
But more often than not, caped adventures
simply act as a springboard for actors to

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:02.559
reach greater heights.

00:01:02.559 --> 00:01:06.890
Chris Evans was Captain America before he
directed his own film; Mary Jane Watson was

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:11.439
an important step towards Kirsten Dunst becoming
a legendary actress; and Wolverine gave Hugh

00:01:11.439 --> 00:01:15.070
Jackman the chance to eventually make some
of his dream musical projects.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:19.360
Often, capes and cowls are what you start
with — not necessarily what you aim for.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:23.619
So it's not every day that an actor like Joaquin
[ Phoenix steps up to play a denizen of Gotham

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:24.140
City.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:28.160
Phoenix has won Grammy awards, been nominated
three times for Oscars, and garnered acclaim

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.580
across multiple genres and mediums.

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:35.649
From The Master to Gladiator to his soundtrack
work for Walk the Line, he's time and time

00:01:35.649 --> 00:01:38.700
again proved his worth as an artist with vision,
passion, and drive.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:43.340
Phoenix isn't just a star you can count on
to play a role well — he's someone you can

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:44.800
count on to make it his own.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:50.280
To say that DC's cinematic universe has encountered
a few rough patches here and there would be

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.200
an understatement, to say the least.

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:57.060
Even the franchise's flagship movies, such
as Batman v Superman and Suicide Squad, tend

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:59.270
to attract more criticism than than praise.

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:03.860
It's not all bad, of course — Shazam! has
practically reinvigorated the franchise and

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:07.700
both Wonder Woman and Aquaman played well
with audiences — but it doesn't exactly

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:08.580
make things easier.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:12.020
Normally, this wouldn't be good news for a
DC movie like Joker.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:15.690
But one benefit of the DC films' troubles
is that they've forced Warner Brothers to

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.360
allow their movies to try new things.

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:22.980
And so it goes for Joker, which is being promoted
as an independent creation inspired by the

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:26.460
DC Universe's mythology — but without having
to obey it entirely.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:30.580
This means the film will be able to take creative
risks and make decisions without having to

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:33.180
make sure it all fits in with the Justice
League timeline.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:38.560
DC's Elseworlds publishing imprint was a similarly-minded
venture that led to the publication of some

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.980
of the best superhero comics ever made.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:45.100
Now, fans will finally get to see how that
experiment translates to the silver screen.

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:50.300
Director Todd Phillips is the guy behind the
Hangover trilogy, first and foremost, but

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:54.720
he's also worked on many films before and
since — from Borat to War Dogs.

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:57.040
Most notably, he's renowned for his work with
comedy.

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:01.960
This works well for Joker, since Phillips
will be a comedian telling a comedian's story.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:06.650
A director well-versed in the kind of gritty
thriller Joker aims to be would be one thing,

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:11.100
but what cinematic alchemy might happen when
the guy behind the camera really understands

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:13.540
what it's like to be inside Arthur Fleck's
head?

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:17.460
The Joker is, at his best, both scary and
funny.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:21.260
And who better to make that terrifying contrast
a reality than a proven jokester?

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:26.570
Gotham City has been subject to countless
differing interpretations over the years.

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:31.290
There's Tim Burton's ultra-stylized neo-Gothic
fantasia, where secretaries have neon signs

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:35.920
in their bedrooms and modern department stores
still advertise with 1950s-style signage.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:40.740
There's also Nolan's mega-city, which is practically
indistinguishable from modern-day Manhattan.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:45.760
Joker, however, seems to be taking a different
tack entirely, with the trailer seemingly

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:49.680
implying that it takes place in a Gotham based
on 1970s New York City.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:53.490
It depicts seedy peep shows clearly riffing
on the Times Square of that era, an Arkham

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:59.050
that Nurse Ratched could have prowled, and
comedy clubs full of that classic '70s mustard-gold-and-brown

00:03:59.050 --> 00:03:59.560
palette.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:03.280
It's a period rarely explored by modern comic
book movies — and one that will doubtless

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:05.280
help Joker stand out from the crowd.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:10.470
Some of the most inventive films of all time
found their success by taking influence from

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:11.240
unexpected places.

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:15.960
For example, Mad Max: Fury Road will likely
go down as one of the greatest action films

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:20.520
of all time — and one of the only to hire
Eve Ensler, of The Vagina Monologues, as a

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:21.040
consultant.

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:25.580
Equally, Guardians of the Galaxy brought new
zest to Marvel by plumbing the depths of 1970s

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:26.280
music.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:27.860
"Dance off, bro.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:29.640
Me versus you."

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:30.980
"It's on!"

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:36.030
And now we have Joker, which Todd Phillips
says will call Martin Scorsese its number

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:40.110
one influence — particularly Raging Bull,
The King of Comedy, and Taxi Driver.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:44.790
Scorsese was actually set to co-produce the
film until he dropped out in 2018, but his

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:48.160
primacy as a figure in the production of the
film doesn't seem to have changed.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:52.340
In a comic book film already full of innovations
and subversions from the norm, the influence

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:55.120
of a great like Scorsese is surely the most
exciting.

